 "note": "Read from the cosmetic list's ext-data heap (one contiguous blob after the 664-byte descriptors, consumed in entry order, ImageListingEntrySize + OtherEntrySize per entry). Entries are selected by CosmeticTypeSymbol (+0x68), which -- like every symbol in this table -- is stored BYTE-REVERSED; selecting by internal-name prefix instead silently drops the `rwd_*` ones. \u26a0 The authored float32 are sRGB-ENCODED, not linear: `tint_neutral_m_default` (\"Black Hole\") authors 0.15/0.9, which as sRGB are #262626 and #e6e6e6 -- near-black and white, matching the game. Read as linear they become a washed-out mid-grey pair (#6c6c6c/#f3f3f3), which is how every tint ended up too weak. `*_linear` is the converted value a renderer wants; `*_hex` is the direct byte encoding. A tint is 6 float32: PrimaryColor RGB then SecondaryColor RGB. The cosmetic editor's UI swaps the two when it shows them, so its 'primary' swatch is this `secondary` field, which is also the colour the menu thumbnail is mostly made of. `tint_chassis_default` (\"No Tint\") authors the sentinel (-1,-1,-1).",
